---
title: Transitions
description: How one shot hands over to the next. The dot and the columns are the system’s own, and the same two the site uses between pages — so a film and the site change scene the same way. Fourteen ordinary cuts beside them.
eyebrow: Content creation · Elements
source: src/studio/transition.css · src/motion/transition.css
---
<p>A shot is a layer that covers the frame (<code>im-studio-shot</code>). Stack two, give the second a <code>data-cut</code> and a time, and the cut plays on the frame’s clock. Two are the system’s and nobody else’s:</p>
<ul>
	<li><strong>The dot.</strong> The recording light swells from the middle until it is the whole frame, and the next shot is inside it — the light is what carries you from one scene to the next.</li>
	<li><strong>The columns.</strong> The twelve columns the page is drawn on wipe the next shot in, one after another, left to right.</li>
</ul>
<p>Both are also <a href="/motion/transitions/">page transitions</a> (<code>data-im-transition="dot"</code>, <code>"columns"</code>): the cut in the film and the move between pages are one idea.</p>
